# prompt for creating read me file explaining the code

# I will provide you with a piece of code. Analyze it and create a short, clear README section explaining what the code does.

# Follow these guidelines:
# - Explain the purpose of the code in simple, non-technical language wherever possible.
# - Break the explanation into short bullet points.
# - Mention the main functionality and important steps.
# - Explain what goes in (input) and what comes out (output), if relevant.
# - Avoid unnecessary technical jargon and lengthy explanations.
# - Do not explain every line of code.
# - Do not make assumptions about functionality that is not present in the code.
# - Keep the explanation brief, clean, and easy for a beginner to understand.

# **Output format:**
# - Use a suitable heading.
# - Write 3–6 concise bullet points.
# - Keep the entire explanation short enough to fit comfortably in a README.md file.

# Return only the README content in Markdown format, without additional commentary.

